  "outcome": "unsupported",
  "detail": "bazel could not fetch its module registry: the JVM rejected the TLS certificate for bcr.bazel.build (PKIX path building failed). bazelisk downloads its own JDK, whose trust store is not /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt, so an extra CA trusted by the image is invisible to it. This is a property of this network, NOT of tcmalloc or of Bazel 8.6.0. On an unproxied host the build proceeds; here it needs a JDK in the image and the CA in that JDK's cacerts.",
